Icons
description: TOC and tab glyphs - Unicode, a few drawn SVGs, picked by format then type
- >
  The TOC row and the matching representation tab share one mark, so a chapter in the tree
  and the `chapter` tab read as the same thing. Almost every mark is a **Unicode character**
  (emoji or a punctuation glyph) in `tools/server/src/client/icons.ts` - the OS emoji font
  draws it, so macOS and Windows look different. A handful of tab views have **no** fitting
  character; those are line-style SVGs in `tools/server/src/client/tab-icons.tsx` (graph,
  thumbnails, large/small icons, details). A fragment is a CSS-drawn selection box
  (`.frag-icon`), not a character.
- >
  Pick order: a node's `format` wins, then a directory
  [concrete](*::language:concretes) (`dir` / `dir/.yo`), else its
  [type](*::language:logical-graph:values). An untagged node's type is the
  [cube](*::meta:facets) **lower bound** from what is actually there - a self-value plus
  keyed fields is `vmap`, not `omni`. `omni` is only the top corner (self + both member kinds).
- Types
  - >
    The self-value types from [values](*::language:logical-graph:values), plus the
    [cube](*::meta:facets) / [members](*::language:logical-graph:members) corners. Structure
    glyphs are the yamlover flow brackets (`{}` `[]` `()` `[]()`), drawn monospaced.
  - !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
    header:
      - Icon
      - Type
      - Notes
        width: 2
    - - '{}'
      - map
      - 'Keyed members only. Alias `object`.'
    - - '[]'
      - seq
      - 'Ordinal members only. Alias `array`.'
    - - '()'
      - kseq
      - 'Keyed + ordinal, no self - flow fields (`!!mix`).'
    - - '{=}'
      - vmap
      - 'Self-value + keyed members, no ordinal.'
    - - '[=]'
      - vseq
      - 'Self-value + ordinal members, no keyed.'
    - - '[]()'
      - omni
      - 'Self-value + both member kinds - flow omni (`[self](fields)`).'
    - - '“”'
      - str
      - 'Unicode text. Alias `string`. A format (below) replaces this.'
    - - '#'
      - int
      - 'A whole number. Alias `integer`.'
    - - ½
      - float
      - 'Any number. Alias `number`.'
    - - ◧
      - bool
      - '`true` / `false`. Alias `boolean`.'
    - - ∅
      - 'null'
      - 'The singleton.'
    - - 0110
      - binary
      - 'Opaque bytes - drawn as bits in a little square, not an emoji.'
- Directories
  - !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
    header:
      - Icon
      - Concrete
      - Notes
        width: 2
    - - 📁
      - '`dir`'
      - 'A plain OS folder - no `.yo/` overlay.'
    - - 🗂️
      - '`dir/.yo` · `dir/index.yo`'
      - 'A yamlover entity stored as a directory.'
- JSON Schema formats
  - >
    Exact names from JSON Schema's `format` vocabulary. Same glyph is reused across aliases
    (`uri` / `iri` / `url` are all 🔗).
  - !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
    header:
      - Icon
      - Format
    - - 🕑
      - '`date-time` · `time`'
    - - 📅
      - '`date`'
    - - ⏳
      - '`duration`'
    - - ✉️
      - '`email` · `idn-email`'
    - - 🖥️
      - '`hostname` · `idn-hostname`'
    - - 🌐
      - '`ipv4` · `ipv6`'
    - - 🔗
      - '`uri` · `iri` · `url` · `*-reference` · `uri-template`'
    - - 🆔
      - '`uuid`'
    - - 🔣
      - '`regex`'
    - - 📍
      - '`json-pointer` · `relative-json-pointer`'
    - - 🔑
      - '`password`'
    - - 🎨
      - '`color`'
- Media and yamlover formats
  - >
    MIME types and `x-yamlover-*` names - prefix match unless listed exact. The
    [format chapter](*::language:logical-graph:format) is what the name *means*; this table is
    only the mark the TOC shows.
  - !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
    header:
      - Icon
      - Format
      - Notes
        width: 2
    - - §
      - '`x-yamlover-chapter`'
      - 'A chapter - the section sign, also the tab.'
    - - 🏷️
      - '`x-yamlover-onto`'
      - 'A tag / taxonomy node.'
    - - 🧩
      - other '`x-yamlover-*`'
      - 'A custom renderer the tables above did not name.'
    - - (box)
      - '`x-yamlover-fragment`'
      - 'Drawn `.frag-icon` - a handled selection with a centre plus.'
    - - 📕
      - '`application/pdf`'
      - ''
    - - 📘
      - '`application/x-fictionbook+xml`'
      - FB2
    - - 📗
      - '`application/epub+zip`'
      - EPUB
    - - 📓
      - '`image/vnd.djvu`'
      - DjVu
    - - 🖼️
      - '`image/*`'
      - 'Any other image.'
    - - 📝
      - '`text/markdown`'
      - ''
    - - 📃
      - '`text/asciidoc`'
      - ''
    - - ▦
      - '`text/csv` · TSV · xls · xlsx'
      - 'A table / workbook.'
    - - 📊
      - '`text/x-plantuml`'
      - 'Source that compiles to a diagram.'
    - - 📄
      - '`text/*` · rtf · doc · docx'
      - 'Plain or office prose the rows above did not claim.'
    - - 🗺️
      - KML · KMZ
      - 'A map overlay.'
    - - 🔊
      - '`audio/*`'
      - ''
    - - 🎬
      - '`video/*`'
      - ''
    - - 💾
      - '`int32/le` · `float64` · …'
      - 'A packed numeric concrete, shown when it still rides as a format.'
- Tabs only
  - >
    A few representation tabs add a mark the TOC never uses, or replace the Unicode one with
    a drawn SVG. Source: `registry.tsx` `icon:` and `tab-icons.tsx`.
  - !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
    header:
      - Icon
      - Tab
      - Notes
        width: 2
    - - ☑
      - task
      - '`x-yamlover-task` - a chapter with a planning strip.'
    - - ✍
      - marklower
      - 'The default chapter-chunk prose.'
    - - ∑
      - latex
      - ''
    - - ⌨
      - plaintext
      - 'Verbatim bytes / encoding picker.'
    - - ▥
      - tag board
      - 'The board explorer.'
    - - (svg)
      - graph
      - 'Drawn DAG - boxes and ranks, `GraphIcon`.'
    - - (svg)
      - thumbnails · large icons · small icons · details
      - 'The explorer family - `ThumbnailsIcon`, `LargeIconsIcon`, `SmallIconsIcon`, `DetailsIcon`.'
